{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/fred2005-formal-groups/blocks/def-strong-multiplicativity","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:strong-multiplicativity","kind":"definition","title":"Strong multiplicativity","uses":["papers/fred2005-formal-groups/blocks/def-skewed-poisson-structure"],"cites":["references/leitner2006"],"tags":["strong-multiplicativity","comultiplication","poisson"],"leanRef":"fred2005:Fred2005.StrongMult.IsStronglyMultiplicative","text":"strong-multiplicativity.md","leanSource":"strong-multiplicativity.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:strong-multiplicativity\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T</code> be a splay with coordinate algebras <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A_i</code>, with a strongly\nfiltered <a href=\"#def:skewed-poisson-structure\" data-at=\"formal-groups-chapter/skewed-poisson\">Poisson structure</a> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\pi</code>, and let\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\cdot</code> denote the multiplication of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">S = \\bigotimes_i A_i</code> (transported to\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T</code> through a choice of ordering <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">&#x3C;</code> on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">I</code>). A map\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Delta \\colon T \\to T \\otimes T</code> is <strong>strongly multiplicative</strong> with respect\nto <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">&#x3C;</code> if</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\Delta \\circ \\pi \\;=\\; (\\cdot \\otimes \\pi \\;+\\; \\pi \\otimes \\cdot \\;+\\; \\pi \\otimes \\pi)\n  \\circ (1 \\otimes \\tau \\otimes 1) \\circ \\Delta,</code></pre>\n<p>where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tau</code> is the flip of tensor factors, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\pi</code> is read as a map\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T \\otimes T \\to T</code>, and the rightmost <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Delta</code> acts on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T \\otimes T</code> as\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Delta \\otimes \\Delta</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Consequence</strong> (<span class=\"cite\" data-keys=\"leitner2006\">[leitner2006]</span>, Proposition 1.13). If each <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A_i</code> carries\nan algebra map <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Delta_i \\colon A_i \\to A_i \\otimes A_i</code> and the induced\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Delta</code> on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T</code> is strongly multiplicative, then <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Delta</code> descends to an\nalgebra map <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">U \\to U \\otimes U</code> on the quotient\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">U = T / (fg - gf - \\pi(f, g))</code> of\n<a href=\"#thm:skew-poisson-integrates\" data-at=\"formal-groups-chapter/integration-theorem\">the integration theorem</a>.</p>\n<p>Reference: <span class=\"cite\" data-keys=\"leitner2006\">[leitner2006]</span>, Definition 1.11 and Proposition 1.13.</p>\n","source":"folio/fred2005-formal-groups/formal-groups-chapter/strong-multiplicativity.md","heading":"Definition","number":"1.2.2","page":"b/def-strong-multiplicativity","qa":{"counts":{"pass":77,"fail":1,"warn":2,"na":18,"unknown":0,"stale":75}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"fred2005:Fred2005.StrongMult.IsStronglyMultiplicative","via":"sibling","path":"folio/fred2005-formal-groups/formal-groups-chapter/strong-multiplicativity.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
